it's for card animation VFX implementation. let me know if that's okay to make a PR later.", "channel": "D0770ET6WBW", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0006_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759173857.856219", "type": "message", "text": "Hello! I don't have any time to test today. But I'll test it tomorrow", "channel": "D0770ET6WBW", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0026_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759173860.807449", "type": "message", "text": "Thank you!", "channel": "D0770ET6WBW", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0026_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759173921.310649", "type": "message", "text": "Okay sure, no problem .. I was fixing some issues I encountered myself .. couldn't trigger it before  :[USERNAME_7156]:", "channel": "D0770ET6WBW", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0006_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759173965.252559", "type": "message", "text": "No problem :))", "channel": "D0770ET6WBW", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0026_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759173978.039839", "type": "message", "text": "it looks great on the video", "channel": "D0770ET6WBW", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0026_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759182470.776769", "type": "message", "text": "Que ondas... ahorita estaba viendo lo del queue manager para win&amp;collect... vi que mandaste otro PR :[USERNAME_35910]:", "channel": "D05S1S2H55M", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0006_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759183084.716429", "type": "message", "text": "Algo asi quedarian, estos 3 escenarios con animaciones + el daily login", "channel": "D05S1S2H55M", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0006_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759184051.940409", "type": "message", "text": "Si pero no creo que te afecte lo que hice", "channel": "D05S1S2H55M", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0021_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759184077.910139", "type": "message", "text": "Se ve un poco mas lento todo", "channel": "D05S1S2H55M", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0021_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759184083.537929", "type": "message", "text": "Pero mas ordenado, eso si", "channel": "D05S1S2H55M", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0021_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759184148.907519", "type": "message", "text": "Eso te quería preguntar si puedo reducir el tiempo del win&amp;collect reward", "channel": "D05S1S2H55M", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0006_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759184193.487389", "type": "message", "text": "Porque debo esperar hasta que termine y que de el reward", "channel": "D05S1S2H55M", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0006_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759184259.923009", "type": "message", "text": "Ay olvidalo.. ya vi.. yo la habia cagado [USERNAME_3855]", "channel": "D05S1S2H55M", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0006_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759184269.612329", "type": "message", "text": "lo habia subido de 0.5 a 1.5 xd", "channel": "D05S1S2H55M", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0006_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759184360.724499", "type": "message", "text": "", "channel": "D05S1S2H55M", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0006_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759186772.164079", "type": "message", "text": "[USERNAME_35162]", "channel": "D05S1S2H55M", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0021_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759186790.799109", "type": "message", "text": "Ya se ve mejor, pero ahi que te digan ellos que pex", "channel": "D05S1S2H55M", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0021_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759252212.611349", "type": "message", "text": "yo on today's main build the pass icon glow stays on after i claimed everything", "channel": "D05U73FNDDL", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0002_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759252231.208739", "type": "message", "text": "saw it 3 levels in a row. its not the vfx, the animation itself is fine, its just the glow", "channel": "D05U73FNDDL", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0002_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759260806.118549", "type": "message", "text": "flow sheet is up to date. the ticket keys are in it where I opened one", "channel": "D06UPGF5PQV", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0012_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759264784.871309", "type": "message", "text": "Hello!", "channel": "D0770ET6WBW", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0026_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759264805.214409", "type": "message", "text": "Before Thursday's flow review I want the queue manager to be a real epic. Right now it is one ticket, and Vincent's flow pass is a sheet on its own. I left a note on the ticket about how I want it. One child for each area, and every report gets its line under the right child. Please also put a stock-take sheet in your ZM queue manager folder and share it with everyone on the review invite, Leonard too, and add one slide with the numbers to your queue manager deck. When it is done tell me here how many reports are passed, how many wait on QA, how many wait on a fix, how many areas are clear and how many reports are on the review list.", "channel": "D0770ET6WBW", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0026_SLACK_ID"}], "has_more": false, "total_count": 66, "response_metadata": {"next_cursor": ""}}

{"ok": true, "messages": [{"ts": "1759249488.495439", "type": "message", "text": "i think we should squeeze in the fix for that issue if it's an easy fix. annoying and players can see that for 10 times in a day if they make it that far.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0012_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1759249488.495439"}, {"ts": "1758905363.341129", "type": "message", "text": "<@EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID> <@EMPLOYEE_0032_SLACK_ID> The iOS memory seems like a guess. Will LiveOps to addressables do the trick you think? Do we have to go after the objects and monsters?

I should note that we currently don't have addressables in ZM. We will need to set up the addressable manager stuff from DD. So There is some more lifting than just making things into an addressable.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758905363.341129"}, {"ts": "1758903616.346579", "type": "message", "text": "After I skipped the zombie lane tutorial, ı got the exception and skipping couldn’t claim the ice cream. <@EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID>   ", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0012_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758903616.346579"}, {"ts": "1758827960.705049", "type": "message", "text": "and both colliders are equal", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758827946.430599", "type": "message", "text": "I was able to see this one in my first play", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758827933.392849", "type": "message", "text": "which may cause performance issues as the colliders are quite complex", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758827921.413599", "type": "message", "text": "looks like we can have objects that have more than 1 click collider", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758827895.596809", "type": "message", "text": "", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758823160.030389", "type": "message", "text": "It could very well be an OS bug that we can't fix.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758823142.221059", "type": "message", "text": "I think on Samsung devices, when you trigger that prompt, or about to, it disables the audio, because the permission dialog is an OS window, and it's an equivalent of homing out. So the app thinks it's in the background, at least from an audio standpoint", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758823108.379949", "type": "message", "text": "OK Fortress Merge also has the weird sound bug. So I was playing, and suddenly my audio disappears... I don't know why, nothing happened on screen. Then I force quit and restart my app, the moment I restart, I get the Push notification permission prompt.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758767858.307829", "type": "message", "text": "Yeah go for it. Once it’s merged we can trigger a testflight build and then can submit to Apple. It will take a few days to go live ", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0038_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758765800.031519", "type": "message", "text": "do you think we can update the build version that the players are testing so we can gather new data?", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758765779.197199", "type": "message", "text": "and also added a skip tutorial button that appears after 10 seconds in the same tutorial step", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758765741.130789", "type": "message", "text": "meaning the tutorial isnt showing anymore and the player is free to play", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758765726.644559", "type": "message", "text": "Not in the logs... I added a new analytics event that is invoked when the tutorial object is destroyed", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758763902.253029", "type": "message", "text": "<@EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID> Any updates on the bugs? See anything strange?", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758751463.920129", "type": "message", "text": "it’s a known thing that some event packs get dropped for some users occasioanlly, it happens to every game every user. It’s supposed to be a small percent but it happens - just a reminder on this", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0038_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758751463.920129"}, {"ts": "1758746963.720009", "type": "message", "text": "And it's evident There was a restart because of the login and splash screen after level 2, but the left_level 2 event never fired off, so it would suggest that it's a pretty severe crash that the app can't even send off anything", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758746963.720009"}, {"ts": "1758746923.853549", "type": "message", "text": "This tells me There was a gap in their log, like Leonard's friend", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758746915.653289", "type": "message", "text": "I think something at the start of a level is crashing people, this user, started level 3, didn't finish level 3, but they have a begin level 2 event, but no left level 2 event, despite being able to start level 3:", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758744890.526289", "type": "message", "text": "Invisible button", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758744887.062759", "type": "message", "text": "Time based, I dont know", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758744881.531029", "type": "message", "text": "And something that allows them to skip tutorial", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741900.550579", "type": "message", "text": "<@EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID> can you add track item match too?", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758741305.545019", "subtype": "thread_broadcast"}, {"ts": "1758741639.564949", "type": "message", "text": "just to discard the possibility", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741621.195989", "type": "message", "text": "we could even disable tutorials completely", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741498.293709", "type": "message", "text": "Maybe even 50% of the users are hit by this", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741473.290079", "type": "message", "text": "But the gist is that I would say 25% of the players are hit by this issue between level 3, 4, and 5. Once you make it through you're probably gonna be OK. So it's like a filter for buggy users", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741426.226829", "type": "message", "text": "Im adding more events to track correctness of each step that can act as blocker", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741424.791859", "type": "message", "text": "It could be some sort of initialization of something", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741413.330639", "type": "message", "text": "I dont even think it is the FTUE anymore, I might be wrong though", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741413.079659", "type": "message", "text": "But if it says "stop game" or "enemy start", I am unclear as to what happened next", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741399.304189", "type": "message", "text": "I would assume if they quit at "Waiting for highlight to fade", it's likely they didn't get to match a single item", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741334.346719", "type": "message", "text": "Because all these "crashes" it's a bit unclear the FTUE happened, did they just get stuck? Or were they at least able to match some items before restarting", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741305.545019", "type": "message", "text": "<@EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID> <@EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID> Is There a good way to just record actual item click on or a set of item was removed from the board as an event? And we just plug it into level 1-5", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758741305.545019"}, {"ts": "1758738754.255909", "type": "message", "text"